body:
## 功能描述 / Feature Description

Add experimental support for the [InferenceX AgentX](https://inferencex.semianalysis.com/agentx) workload to EvalScope Perf.

AgentX is a serving-performance workload derived from long-context, multi-turn coding-agent traces. It preserves request lengths, prefix-sharing structure, think time, and main-agent/subagent dependencies while replacing private content with synthetic tokens. It evaluates serving throughput, interactivity, latency, and KV/prefix-cache behavior rather than model answer quality.

## 需求背景 / Background

EvalScope Perf already supports synthetic multi-turn workloads and flat request-trace replay. AgentX adds a different workload shape:

- a request DAG containing main-agent and subagent chains;
- closed-loop concurrency defined as active session trees rather than fixed in-flight HTTP requests;
- trajectory warmup and prefix-cache reconstruction;
- session recycling with cache busting;
- long-context 256K and 1M variants;
- scenario-specific result validity and provenance requirements.

Representing AgentX as only a regular dataset plugin would not preserve these semantics. The official replay logic is already implemented in [AIPerf](https://github.com/ai-dynamo/aiperf), including the inferencex-agentx-mvp scenario.

## 预期行为 / Expected Behavior

Introduce AgentX as a dedicated Perf scenario backed by a pinned and isolated AIPerf runner, instead of reimplementing the workload scheduler in EvalScope.

A first-stage integration could:

- provide an agentx scenario entry point in EvalScope Perf;
- invoke a user-provided or isolated compatible AIPerf executable;
- support the official full and 256K datasets;
- validate model, tokenizer, endpoint, context length, duration, concurrency, and GPU metadata;
- preserve raw AIPerf artifacts;
- import key AgentX metrics into a dedicated Pydantic result model;
- record AIPerf version/commit, dataset revision, seed, warmup/profile settings, model/server/hardware metadata, and validity status;
- clearly distinguish short smoke runs from canonical comparable AgentX runs.

Example proposed interface:

    evalscope perf \
      --scenario agentx \
      --url http://localhost:8000/v1/chat/completions \
      --model MODEL \
      --tokenizer-path TOKENIZER \
      --agentx-variant 256k \
      --parallel 8 \
      --duration 3600 \
      --num-gpus 8

The exact CLI and result schema should follow existing EvalScope Perf conventions during implementation.

## Scope / Non-goals

In scope:

- AIPerf execution and version checks;
- configuration validation;
- raw artifact retention;
- AgentX-specific result normalization and provenance;
- direct-AIPerf versus EvalScope-wrapper parity tests;
- documentation for smoke and canonical runs.

Out of scope for the initial integration:

- reimplementing the AgentX DAG scheduler or Weka trace loader;
- treating AgentX as a model-quality benchmark;
- claiming official comparability for shortened or modified runs;
- reproducing the full InferenceX telemetry dashboard.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] EvalScope can launch a pinned compatible AIPerf AgentX run without adding AIPerf to the default Perf runtime dependency set.
- [ ] Full and 256K dataset variants are selectable and their revisions are recorded.
- [ ] Raw AIPerf output is retained unchanged.
- [ ] Normalized output records request accounting, throughput, TTFT/E2EL/ITL/TPOT or interactivity metrics when present, errors, and per-GPU metadata.
- [ ] Missing metrics remain unavailable rather than being reported as zero.
- [ ] Output records whether a run is canonical/comparable and explains every invalid condition.
- [ ] A mock-server smoke test covers command construction, output parsing, error handling, and secret redaction.
- [ ] A parity test shows that wrapping AIPerf does not change the effective scenario parameters or reported raw results.
- [ ] User documentation explains AgentX concurrency, warmup, long-context requirements, and the difference between smoke and canonical runs.

## 其他信息 / Additional Information

Relevant references:

- [AgentX methodology](https://inferencex.semianalysis.com/agentx/methodology)
- [AgentX full dataset](https://huggingface.co/datasets/semianalysisai/cc-traces-weka-062126)
- [AgentX 256K dataset](https://huggingface.co/datasets/semianalysisai/cc-traces-weka-062126-256k)
- [AIPerf AgentX tutorial](https://docs.nvidia.com/aiperf/dev/tutorials/datasets-inputs/inference-x-agent-x-mvp-benchmark)
- [InferenceX architecture](https://github.com/SemiAnalysisAI/InferenceX/blob/main/docs/architecture.md)

A native implementation may be reconsidered only if EvalScope intentionally wants to replace AIPerf and is prepared to maintain workload-format and scheduler parity as the upstream scenario evolves.
